<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Black Army of Hungary</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1460s–<a href="/years/1494">1494</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Black Army</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Black Army was the standing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> army of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthias-corvinus">Matthias Corvinus</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, built up from the 1460s. Made up of Czech, German, Polish, Serbian and Hungarian soldiers, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heavy-cavalry">heavy cavalry</a>, light hussars, handgunners and Hussite-style wagon forts, it won <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, Silesia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> for Matthias. Left unpaid after his death in 1490, it was disbanded in the early 1490s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/black-army-of-hungary.jpg" alt="Black Army of Hungary" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Black_Army_of_Hungary.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
